            "issue": "The notes disclose the irregular printed ὑπολῆσαι, but they do not establish a lexical or morphological account supporting “recover from.” The regular aorist infinitive of ὑπολήγω would be ὑπολῆξαι, the conjecture identified in the notes. Moreover, cessation or abatement does not by itself establish the draft’s particular representation of the inhabitants as recovering from the effects of Simon’s slander. The context suggests diminishing hostility, but that contextual expectation is not sufficient evidence for this specific rendering of the surviving verb. The eleven-dot lacuna is faithfully preserved and is not the reason for the block.",
